        "prefix_token_count": 36,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Identify the equations of the asymptotes given: \\( y = 2x - 3 \\) and \\( y = 17 - 2x \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 382,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 384,
        "char_start": 97,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 134,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 135,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Recognize that the equations of the asymptotes for a hyperbola centered at \\((h, k)\\) with slopes \\(\\pm \\frac{b}{a}\\) can be written as \\( y - k = \\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x - h) \\). From the given asymptotes, we can see that the slopes are \\(\\pm 2\\), indicating that \\(\\frac{b}{a} = 2\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 787,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 789,
        "char_start": 386,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 286,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 287,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: The center of the hyperbola is the intersection of the asymptotes. To find the center, solve the system of equations:\n\\[ y = 2x - 3 \\]\n\\[ y = 17 - 2x \\]\n\nSet the right sides equal to each other:\n\\[ 2x - 3 = 17 - 2x \\]\n\\[ 4x = 20 \\]\n\\[ x = 5 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( x = 5 \\) back into one of the original equations to find \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 2(5) - 3 = 7 \\]\n\nSo, the center of the hyperbola is \\((5, 7)\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1023,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1025,
        "char_start": 791,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 378,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 379,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Since the slopes of the asymptotes are \\(\\pm 2\\), the hyperbola is oriented horizontally, and its equation can be written as:\n\\[ \\frac{(x-5)^2}{a^2} - \\frac{(y-7)^2}{b^2} = 1 \\]\nGiven \\(\\frac{b}{a} = 2\\), we have \\( b = 2a \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1283,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1285,
        "char_start": 1027,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 508,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 509,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Substitute the point \\((4, 7)\\) into the hyperbola's equation to find \\(a\\):\n\\[ \\frac{(4-5)^2}{a^2} - \\frac{(7-7)^2}{(2a)^2} = 1 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{1}{a^2} - 0 = 1 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{1}{a^2} = 1 \\]\n\\[ a^2 = 1 \\]\n\\[ a = 1 \\]\nSince \\( b = 2a \\), we have \\( b = 2 \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1497,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1498,
        "char_start": 1287,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 598,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 599,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Calculate the distance between the foci using the relationship \\( c^2 = a^2 + b^2 \\):\n\\[ c^2 = 1^2 + 2^2 = 1 + 4 = 5 \\]\n\\[ c = \\sqrt{5} \\]\n\nThe distance between the foci is \\( 2c \\):\n\\[ 2c = 2\\sqrt{5} \\]"
      }
